From 6d311efb762362a2c447c9ea6d2482a54bdbbbf2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zambia Treasury Insight <patch@local>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:33:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] Tier 2 #7: T-bills/bonds auction yields + overnight
 rates connector

Adds 11 new series extracted from the Bank of Zambia fortnightly statistics
release (the user-provided Excel attachments):

  T-bills (weekly auction yields):
    TBILL_91D, TBILL_182D, TBILL_273D, TBILL_364D  (2013-01 -> 2017-05)

  GRZ bonds (weekly auction yields):
    BOND_3Y, BOND_5Y, BOND_7Y, BOND_10Y, BOND_15Y  (2013-01 -> 2017-05)

  Overnight rates:
    ON_INTERBANK  (daily, 2012-04 -> 2026-11, last obs of each day)
    ON_LENDING    (sparse, 2020-11 -> 2026-09, rate-change dates only)

Implementation:

  * app/config.py: registers the 11 new series with native freq, kind, plausible
    ranges, and generous jump-flags (auction yields move sharply between auctions).
  * app/connectors/manual_csv.py: now supports a LONG-format CSV layout
    (date,tenor,value) in addition to the existing wide format. One file
    (TBILL_BOND_WEEKLY.csv) produces many series. Wide-format files take
    precedence: a tenor with its own <SERIES_ID>.csv is skipped in long-format
    files (so POLICY_RATE.csv stays authoritative over the policy_rate column
    in the yields sheet).
  * app/ingest.py: run_live() now MERGES manual backfill data with live feed
    data for the same series (live wins on overlapping dates, live source
    attribution preserved). This lets data/manual/USDZMW.csv (BoZ daily mid-rate
    2001-2026) extend the live Frankfurter feed's history without overriding
    recent values.
  * data/manual/: ships 5 new CSVs (TBILL_BOND_WEEKLY.csv, TBILL_BOND_MONTHLY.csv,
    ON_INTERBANK.csv, ON_LENDING.csv, USDZMW.csv) with # source: headers.

72 tests passing (2 updated to reflect the new merge-and-extend behavior).
